<title>CHINA: China Jan-Oct energy investment up 16.7 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>China Jan-Oct energy investment up 16.7 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total investment in China's energy sector rose 16.7 percent to 182.5 billion yuan ($21.99 billion) in January-October compared to the year-ago period, the official Xinhua news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>Investment in power generation was 111.0 billion yuan during the period, up a year-on-year 26.7 percent, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>Funds pumped into petroleum inched up 0.8 percent to 55.0 billion yuan, it said without giving further details. ($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
</text>
